{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Investigation 2026-10-24 22:50 PDT (read-only; no code changed, not claimed yet). Candidate mechanism, from code reading plus one measurement; not yet reproduced with an instrumented sweep. (1) compact_all_cli builds one position->commit map before locking (_sweep_position_map). If that returns None/empty (git failure, or map misses), the fold path calls _build_authorship_ledger (src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py) INSIDE the store write lock. For each signed event with no map hit it runs authorship.resolve_event_commit (ticket-scoped git log --full-history), and if that returns None, authorship.resolve_position_commit (src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py): a STORE-WIDE 'git log --diff-filter=A --full-history --no-renames -- *<position>-*.json' with a 30 s timeout. (2) Measured on this operator host's tickets clone (300,142 commits, host load about 12): the store-wide walk for one real event position took 140.42 s and 142.43 s on two runs, so on a clone this size it always hits the 30 s timeout, i.e. each map-miss costs up to 30 s per event, twice if the ticket-scoped walk also fails, all while holding the lock. That matches the observed 91-181 s waits, 33 m 46 s and 11 m sweeps, and git log --full-history children under the lock holder. (3) The between-ticket yield (_sweep_should_yield -> write_lock_is_busy) only sees a CURRENT HOLDER, not a writer waiting to acquire, so it cannot shorten a long single-ticket fold. Not established: how often the map is empty or misses on the production server, and the 300k-commit figure is this host's clone, not the server's (the 28,570-commit lineage ticket 3394 is a candidate reason the clone is large). Proposed next steps: instrument a sweep against a copy of the store to count map misses and lock hold time per ticket; fix by never running unbounded git walks under the lock (resolve commits before taking it, or store null and fill later) and bounding the in-lock work; regression test with a fake git that sleeps."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792906805852649001,"uuid":"d91d7032-8a8d-4c57-a567-187a9a8912fb"}